    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T10:02:59Z",
    "body": "**Design note from the maker's Gen3 instructions (read 2026-11-11; local reference only):** a plate-mounted modular vise of this kind is **two separate jaw blocks**, a fixed side and an adjustable side, each bolted to plate holes and pinned against the plate's bores. The opening is set by which holes each side uses. The adjustable side is pushed up to the workpiece as a spacer, then clamped with its side bolts. So model it as **two jaw-block fixtures placed on the #819 grid** (a fixed and an adjustable block, plus an optional dual-station variant), fitted so the adjustable block touches the stock, rather than as a style of the screw-vise body. Generic dimensions only.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
